## What’s New in SoundDash 2.0

- Route your Mac’s audio to compatible AirPlay speakers without changing its selected audio output.
- Connect up to five AirPlay speakers at once and see each speaker’s connection status.
- Test AirPlay speakers directly. Pairing codes are saved for future connections.
- Add an output from the bottom of the output list.
- Save synchronization settings to stop the test while keeping audio routing active.
- AirPlay routes are now clearly labeled as Mac-connected or direct, and unassigned outputs are automatically removed when routing starts.
- Save up to 10 named profiles with audio routing and sound settings, then switch between them from the dashboard or menu bar.
- Profile edits are saved automatically. Choose Edit Profile to open the selected profile’s Audio Routing page.
- Choose built-in EQ presets or save up to 10 custom presets. Load, rename, delete, or update a preset, or save your changes as a new preset.
- Export and import your current setup and saved profiles between Macs. Matching devices are selected automatically where possible; review any unresolved devices during import.
